 7. 🎓 South&#x27;s student surge 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data : National Center for Education Statistics. Chart: Erin Davis/Axios Visuals America's future college pipeline is growing in the South and shrinking elsewhere, Axios' Russell Contreras reports. 

 By 2041, the number of high school graduates is projected to fall by 29% in California, 27% in New York and 32% in Illinois, per the Western Interstate Commission for Higher Education . The South's high school graduate population is projected to grow 3%. Keep reading . 

 
 
