 8. 🧶 1 for the road: Cash for crafting 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Americans of all ages are spending more than ever on offline hobbies and crafts, and are increasingly willing to cut elsewhere or dip into their savings, Bloomberg reports ( $ ). 

 Sofia Szyfer, a 25-year-old New York publicist, told Bloomberg she's spending almost $300 every month on stickers, paper goods and craft-related events. She's a devotee of "junk journaling" — a mix of scrapbooking, collage and diary-keeping. Szyfer has cut back on other forms of entertainment: "I'd rather just go and spend $50 on stickers than go to a live event or a live concert." 
 
